# Who reviews what.
#
# Two maintainers own every path. `main` requires one approving review from a code owner who is
# not the author, so each maintainer reviews the other's changes, and either one can review a
# contributor's. Without this file a PR opens with no requested reviewer.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all is FIRST and the per-area lines below it are the
# ones GitHub actually reports. They are spelled out per package and per app on purpose: the day a
# second maintainer takes one area, the change is one owner on one line, not a new file.

*                          @divshekhar @imheadrick

